            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="0422" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13550: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-25T16:00:00+08:00">July 25, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 25—1:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Shanghai and Tokyo please inform Japanese authorities [that] committee of 4
                    missions including 2 American missions proposes establishment safety zone
                    Ichang, Hupeh, at Catholic Convent 2 kilometers southeast of city on prominent
                    hill. Convent marked with French, Belgian and Red Cross flags. Maps follow.
                    Local British, French, Belgian Consuls also received notification from
                    committee.</p>
                <p>Sent to Shanghai. Shanghai please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
